#+TITLE: @agenda — Scheduling + planning specialist console
#+SUPERSET_DASHBOARD: agenda-console
#+SUPERSET_DATABASE: org-llm
#+FILETAGS: :template:superset:dashboard:agenda:specialist:
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil

# Specialist console for @agenda (Scheduling + planning specialist). Designed by
# @geordi via deepseek-r1 askbook on 2026-05-07. Each chart's
# metric is verbatim from org_llm/metrics/registry.yaml.

* LLM Call Performance by Model
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: line
:END:

Tracks the average response time of LLM calls by model over time to
identify performance trends and potential bottlenecks.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name llm_call_performance_by_model :metric llm_avg_ms :group_by [model, llm_day]
SELECT model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS llm_day, AVG(duration_ms) AS llm_avg_ms FROM llm_calls GROUP BY model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Crew Action Outcomes
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: area
:END:

Provides a detailed view of crew actions and their outcomes over time,
helping to identify areas of frequent success or failure.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name crew_action_outcomes :metric crew_actions :group_by [crew_action, crew_outcome, crew_day]
SELECT action AS crew_action, outcome AS crew_outcome, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS crew_day, COUNT(*) AS crew_actions FROM crew_log GROUP BY action, outcome, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Historical Command Usage
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: bar
:END:

Shows the frequency of different commands used over time, aiding in
understanding the most common and least used functionalities.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name historical_command_usage :metric hist_command_count :group_by [hist_command, hist_day]
SELECT command AS hist_command, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS hist_day, COUNT(DISTINCT command) AS hist_command_count FROM history GROUP BY command, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Sensor Alert Rate by Probe
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Visualizes the alert rate of different probes over time to quickly
identify which sensors are most active or problematic.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name sensor_alert_rate_by_probe :metric probe_alert_rate :group_by [probe, sensor_day]
SELECT probe, date(ts, 'unixepoch') AS sensor_day, AVG(CASE WHEN status IN ('watch','alert','critical') THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS probe_alert_rate FROM sensor_log GROUP BY probe, date(ts, 'unixepoch')
#+END_SRC
